[a] Immediate mode mov instructions
https://community.arm.com/groups/processors/blog/2010/07/27/how-to-load-constants-in-assembly-for-arm-architecture

movt : move top, will load a 16-bit constant into the top 16 bits of the register while leaving the lower 16 bits untouched

movw : move wide, will load a 16-bit constant into the lower 16bits of the register while zeroing out the upper 16 bits

So its generally adviseable to use movw followed by movt to load any 32-bit constant
========================================================
[b] Constant pool

aka pc relative loads
ldr rd,[#pc, offset]

or use the synthetic instruction
ldr rd,=0x1234234324

Assembler will find the constant pool and put the correct PC relative offset into it
